COMPLIANCE:
Scene ID: SC_006_007
Allowed events: The party arrives at the sanctum entrance, Vance draws aggro at 10 HP, Rhea prepares the Null-Value Token.
Forbidden milestones: null_value_token_crafted (already DONE), overseer_budget_discovered (already DONE).

Current arm-side / inventory facts: 
- Vance holds Rebar in right hand.
- Rhea holds Null-Value Token in left hand.

Durable changes committed: 
- Added milestone: sanctum_threshold_reached = DONE.
- Added status: Aggro Target to Vance.

APPEARANCE_CHECK:
- rhea_mercer: singed arm hair
- vance_harrow: blistered hands
- unit_734: smoking chassis

PROSE:
Rhea clutched the Null-Value Token in her left hand as the party slipped out of the jagged outskirts, their boots crunching softly until they reached the polished marble steps of the sanctum entrance, where two towering, gold-plated guards stood watch. The token felt impossibly heavy, a localized void of light and logic resting against her palm.

[Stamina: 1/150]
[Status Effect: Exhaustion (Severe) - Movement speed reduced by 90%.]

Every breath felt like inhaling ground glass. She leaned against a basalt pillar, her singed arm hair brushing the rough stone. Beside her, Vance tightened his grip on his rusted Rebar. His heavily blistered hands bled sluggishly over the iron, a testament to the brutal attrition of the last hour.

[HP: 10/150]
[Status Effect: Audit Compliance (Red-Tier) active.]

"I step up, they look at me," Vance muttered, his voice barely a rasp. "You do the math."

Behind them, Unit 734 let out a metallic wheeze. Plumes of thick gray exhaust vented from its smoking chassis, the drone struggling to remain hovering.

[Chassis Integrity: 34%]
[Warning: Critical Failure Imminent.]

"Just keep them focused on you," Rhea said, her voice shaking. "If they scan my inventory before I trigger the exploit, the node will delete us both."

The elite bureaucratic guards were perfectly symmetrical, their gold-plated armor etched with scrolling ledgers of System law. They held halberds that hummed with administrative violence.

Vance didn't hesitate. He rolled his shoulders, stepped out from behind the pillar, and slammed the Rebar against the marble stairs. The sharp, metallic crack echoed across the courtyard.

Both guards snapped their featureless visors toward him.

[Aggro Generated: Vance Harrow.]
[Threat Assessment: Hostile. Lethal Force Authorized.]

The air pressure dropped as the guards raised their weapons, their targeting lasers painting Vance's chest. He planted his feet at the threshold, drawing their full aggro, while Rhea stepped out from the shadows, raising the token for the final breach.

